#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:1
msgid "Safe Kernels Using Rust's Type System"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:3
msgid ""
"On a CPU, `rustc` prevents data races through single-thread ownership: one "
"mutable reference, zero aliases. On a GPU, thousands of threads execute the "
"same kernel function at once against the same output buffer, so single-"
"thread borrow checking alone is not enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:5
msgid ""
"`cuda-oxide` closes that gap in **three layers**, so most kernels need zero "
"`unsafe`:"
