#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:19
msgid "Layer 1: Safe by Construction (`DisjointSlice` + `ThreadIndex`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:21
msgid "How `DisjointSlice` prevents cross-thread write races"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:23
msgid ""
"Layer 1 pairs two types so distinct threads never obtain `&mut T` to the "
"same element:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:25
msgid ""
"**`ThreadIndex<'kernel, IndexSpace>`**: An unforgeable witness around a "
"`usize` with no public constructor. It is minted only from hardware "
"registers (`threadIdx`, `blockIdx`, `blockDim`) and is `!Send + !Sync + !"
"Copy + !Clone` with a `'kernel` lifetime, so threads cannot copy it or pass "
"it through shared memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:26
msgid ""
"**`DisjointSlice<T, IndexSpace>`**: A mutable output view whose `get_mut()` "
"accepts only a matching `ThreadIndex` and returns `Option<&mut T>` (`None` "
"when out of bounds)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:28
msgid ""
"use cuda_device::{DisjointSlice, kernel};\n"
"\n"
"#[kernel]\n"
"pub fn vecadd(a: &[f32], b: &[f32], mut c: DisjointSlice<f32>) {\n"
"    if let Some((c_elem, idx)) = c.get_mut_indexed() {\n"
"        let i = idx.get();\n"
"        *c_elem = a[i] + b[i];\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:40
msgid "When you need the index before calling `get_mut`, mint it explicitly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:42
msgid ""
"#[kernel]\n"
"pub fn vecadd(a: &[f32], b: &[f32], mut c: DisjointSlice<f32>) {\n"
"    let idx = thread::index_1d();\n"
"    let i = idx.get();\n"
"    if let Some(c_elem) = c.get_mut(idx) {\n"
"        *c_elem = a[i] + b[i];\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:53
msgid "Why this is race-free end to end:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:55
msgid ""
"**Unique coordinates**: `index_1d()` is unique when grid and block Y/Z "
"dimensions are `1` (enforced on the host by a `domain = 1` `PreparedLaunch`; "
"raw launches with active Y/Z fail closed on device and return `None`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:56
msgid "**Bounds-checked**: Out-of-range threads get `None` from `get_mut()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:57
msgid ""
"**Layout-branded**: `DisjointSlice<T, Index2D<128>>` rejects "
"`ThreadIndex<'_, Index2D<256>>` at compile time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:58
msgid ""
"**Non-transferable**: `!Send + !Sync + !Copy + !Clone` keeps each witness "
"private to the thread that minted it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:60
msgid ""
"1D PreparedLaunch (Y = Z = 1)  ->  unique index_1d per thread  ->  Some(&mut "
"c[i])\n"
"Raw 2D launch (active Y or Z)  ->  invalid witness             ->  None "
"(safe fallback)\n"
msgstr ""

