#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:78
msgid "Check a tile once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:80
msgid ""
"When each thread owns a small fixed tile, `LinearTiles<N>` checks the entire "
"tile in one comparison and serves constant offsets (`at_const::<0>()`) with "
"zero extra checks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:82
msgid ""
"use cuda_device::{DisjointSlice, LinearTiles, kernel, launch_contract, "
"thread};\n"
"\n"
"#[kernel(launch_context = launch_context)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(\n"
"    domain = 1,\n"
"    coordinates = u32,\n"
"    block = (64, 1, 1),\n"
")]\n"
"pub fn add_one(mut values: DisjointSlice<u32, LinearTiles<4>>) {\n"
"    let thread_index = thread::index_1d_u32(launch_context);\n"
"\n"
"    if let Some(mut tile) = values.tile_thread32(thread_index) {\n"
"        let first = tile.at_const::<0>().read();\n"
"        tile.at_const::<0>().write(first + 1);\n"
"\n"
"        let second = tile.at_const::<1>().read();\n"
"        tile.at_const::<1>().write(second + 1);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:104
msgid "How the two attributes cooperate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:106
msgid ""
"**`launch_context`**: Zero-sized token injected into the kernel body "
"carrying the launch contract's static facts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:107
msgid ""
"**`domain = 1, coordinates = u32`**: Unlocks "
"`thread::index_1d_u32(launch_context)` without 64-bit index math."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:108
msgid ""
"**`block = (64, 1, 1)`**: Checked on the host by `prepare_*` *and* emitted "
"into PTX as `.reqntid 64, 1, 1` so the CUDA driver rejects any mismatched "
"raw launch too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:109
msgid ""
"**2D tiles**: Pair `thread::coord_2d_u32(launch_context)` with "
"`RowMajorTiles<ROWS, COLS, ROW_STRIDE>`; see [`proof_carrying_views`]"
"(https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust/tree/main/cuda-oxide/crates/rustc-"
"codegen-cuda/examples/proof_carrying_views)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:111
msgid "2D strides and launch-uniform scalars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:113
msgid ""
"**Compile-time stride (`Index2D<S>`)**: Prefer this whenever row width `S` "
"is a constant. Mixing strides fails to type-check:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:115
msgid ""
"#[kernel]\n"
"pub fn rejected(mut out: DisjointSlice<u32, Index2D<128>>) {\n"
"    if let Some(idx) = thread::index_2d::<256>() { // compile error: 256 != "
"128\n"
"        if let Some(slot) = out.get_mut(idx) { *slot = 1; }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:124
msgid ""
"**Runtime stride (`Runtime2DIndex` and `RowWidth`)**: When matrix width `n` "
"is only known at launch, two threads must never disagree on the stride "
"(thread `(1, 0)` at stride `5` and thread `(0, 5)` at stride `100` both "
"resolve flat slot `5`). Bind the width once on the host so every thread "
"reads the same value from the slice itself:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:126
msgid ""
"// Host: bind row width `n` into `c` once at launch\n"
"module.write_c(&stream, &prepared, cuda_host::RowWidth::new(&mut c, n))?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:131
msgid ""
"#[kernel(launch_context = lc)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(domain = 2, coordinates = u32, block = (16, 16, 1))]\n"
"pub fn write_c(mut c: DisjointSlice<f32, RuntimeRowMajorTiles<1, 1>>) {\n"
"    let coord = thread::coord_2d_u32(lc);\n"
"    if let Some(mut cell) = c.tile_2d32_rt(coord) {\n"
"        cell.at_const::<0, 0>().write(1.0);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:142
msgid ""
"**Launch-uniform scalars (`Uniform<T>`)**: Wrap scalar parameters as "
"`Uniform<u32>` when every thread must observe the same launch-constant value "
"(`rows.get()`). Host callers still pass a plain `u32`, and device code "
"cannot forge a `Uniform<T>` from thread-varying data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:144
msgid ""
"For hoisting *input* slice bounds checks on `a[...]` and `b[...]` out of "
"inner loops, see [Bounds Checks: Pay Once or Opt Out](bounds-checks.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:148
msgid "Layer 2: Cooperative & Async Kernels (`#[verify]`, preview)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:150
msgid ""
"Layer 1 handles independent per-thread writes, while cooperative GPU kernels "
"share `static mut SharedArray` tiles, stage DMA transfers with `Barrier`, or "
"pass plain `&mut [T]` buffers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:152
msgid ""
"Adding `#[verify(...)]` next to `#[launch_contract(...)]` hands the kernel's "
"`PostMem2Reg` MIR to **Lean 4** at compile time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:154
msgid ""
"#[kernel]\n"
"#[launch_contract(domain = 2, coordinates = u32, block = (16, 16, 1))]\n"
"#[verify(no_oob_idx(TILE_A, TILE_B), no_data_race(TILE_A, TILE_B), "
"uniform_barriers)]\n"
"pub fn sgemm_tiled(a: &[f32], b: &[f32], mut c: DisjointSlice<f32, "
"RuntimeRowMajorTiles<1, 1>>) {\n"
"    static mut TILE_A: SharedArray<f32, 256> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut TILE_B: SharedArray<f32, 256> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    // Direct TILE_A[...] and TILE_B[...] reads/writes with 0 `unsafe` "
"blocks!\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:165
msgid ""
"What `#[verify(...)]` unlocks in safe Rust (zero `unsafe`, zero runtime "
"check overhead):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:167
msgid ""
"**Shared-memory tiling & reductions**: Proves `SharedArray` bounds "
"(`no_oob_idx`), cross-thread race freedom (`no_data_race`), and non-"
"divergent `sync_threads()` (`uniform_barriers`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:168
msgid ""
"**Plain `&mut [T]` parameters**: Unverified `&mut [T]` kernel parameters are "
"rejected at compile time; `#[verify(no_oob_idx(c), disjoint_writes(c))]` "
"proves cross-thread exclusivity and unlocks `&mut [T]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:169
msgid ""
"**Async TMA, warp rings, 2-CTA clusters, and Blackwell `TMEM`**: Proves "
"`mbarrier` token ordering, `SharedArray<Barrier, N>` ring back-pressure, 2-"
"CTA `cluster_sync()` + `map_shared_rank` rank bounds, `CLC` responses, and "
"`tcgen05` + `TMEM` lifecycles (`tmem_lifecycle`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/the-safety-model.md:171
msgid ""
"See [Provably Safe Kernels (preview)](verified-kernels.md) for the full "
"guide and nine runnable examples from `safe_vecadd` to `2.118 PFLOP/s` "
"Blackwell GEMM."
msgstr ""

